  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a matrix AAA consisting of NNN rows and MMM columns.\n\nYou task is to select an element A(x,y)A_{(x, y)}A(x,y)​ (1≤x≤N,1≤y≤M)(1 \\le x \\le N, 1 \\le y \\le M)(1≤x≤N,1≤y≤M) such that the following value is **maximised**:\n\n\n∑i=1,i≠xi=N∑j=1,j≠yj=M(A(i,j)⊕A(x,y))\\sum_{i = 1, i\\neq x}^{i = N} \\sum_{j = 1, j\\neq y}^{j = M} (A_{(i, j)} \\oplus A_{(x, y)})∑i=1,i=xi=N​∑j=1,j=yj=M​(A(i,j)​⊕A(x,y)​). Here, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes bitwise XOR operation.\nIn other words, you need to select an element A(x,y)A_{(x, y)}A(x,y)​ such that the sum of bitwise XOR of A(x,y)A_{(x, y)}A(x,y)​ with all elements that are **not in** the xthx^{th}xth row **or** the ythy^{th}yth column is maximum.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of rows and columns.\nThe next NNN lines contains MMM space-separated integers each, describing the entire matrix.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **maximum sum** possible.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤1051 \\leq M \\leq 10^51≤M≤105",
      "0≤A(i,j)&lt;2300 \\leq A_{(i, j)} \\lt 2^{30}0≤A(i,j)​&lt;230",
      "The sum of N×MN \\times MN×M over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n2 3\n1 2 3\n4 5 6",
        "output": "13",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Consider the element A(2,1)=4A_{(2, 1)} = 4A(2,1)​=4. The sum obtained on selecting this element would be 4⊕2+4⊕3=6+7=134\\oplus 2 + 4 \\oplus 3 = 6+7 = 134⊕2+4⊕3=6+7=13. Note that the elements of second row and first column are omitted while calculating the sum.\nIt can proven that no other element would lead to a sum more than 131313."
      }
    ]
  },
